          "id": 1644980602,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "It is only required that the link-layer type \"be a valid hardware type assigned by the IANA\"\nTheoretically (unlikely, granted), it is possible that the address length is less than six bytes, yes?\n\nShouldn't this be something like testing if `(optlen < 2)` and then adding the string if `optlen > 2`, similar to `DUID_LL`?",
